<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Monroe returns three months after her first visit. She has taken the continuous pill daily and has had no periods, only a day or two of light spotting each month. Her worst pelvic pain in the past week was 4 of 10, from 8, she has used naproxen on two or three days a month, and she has missed no work for two months. Pain with deep intercourse persists and makes her tense up beforehand; bowel movements are no longer painful. The urine culture from her bladder infection grew Escherichia coli sensitive to nitrofurantoin, and her HPV, HIV and hepatitis C tests from the preventive visit were negative. She has had eight therapy sessions, sleeps seven hours without any sleep aid, and feels more like herself. She has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pain</td><td>Worst 4 of 10, from 8; no missed work for two months</td></tr><tr><td>Bleeding</td><td>No periods; light spotting a day or two a month</td></tr><tr><td>Intercourse</td><td>Deep pain persists</td></tr><tr><td>Results</td><td>Urine culture E. coli; HPV, HIV and hepatitis C negative</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 6, GAD-7 5; eight therapy sessions</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

